<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bavarian Palatinate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1816–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bavarian Palatinate was the territory on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> that belonged to the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> from 1816 to 1946, at first called the Rhine District. Formed from former lands of the Electoral Palatinate, the prince-bishopric of Speyer, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zweibrucken">Zweibrücken</a> and other states, it was governed from Speyer. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it became part of the new German state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bavarian-palatinate.jpg" alt="Bavarian Palatinate" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banner_of_the_Palatinate.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
